Z||000000||Monkeyman||01-01-2000||05:06 AM||||Here's a tail light mod for the notchback that I just got done doing.  It is very inexpensive and it looks killer! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The pics don't do it justice.  Let me know if anyone's interested and I'll post details about how I did it.  I'll get some daytime pics tomorrow and post them. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tail_light_mod-1.jpg">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tail_light_mod-2.jpg"> <BR>The text can be changed to almost anything you want such as: one large "Fiero" for those of you who have converted your inner tail light to t.s./brake/marker light, or what about 3 silhouettes (bats, roadrunners, etc?).  I'd really like everyone's opinion on this.  If I provided the precut vinyl, this could be done for less than $30US, I think.||||reg||10
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||01-01-2000||01:03 PM||||That looks cool monkeyman, How easy is it to change to a different design? I was thinking about car club logo ??  like for a car show or club event? It looks like you did a real pro job.||||reg||14
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||01-01-2000||05:33 PM||||Awesome!!!<P>did you remove the grille in the lights? I'd definitely be interested in hearing how you did that mod!<P>Anyone know how well something like this would work on the fastback tail lights?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||01-01-2000||06:00 PM||||HAHAHAHHAHAHAHAHAHHAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHHHHAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA!!!!  That's cute!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||01-01-2000||06:05 PM||||Monkeyman, I remember you talking about doing a tailight mod, but I never thought it would look that good. Looks great. I should have thought of that. Everyone, let's hear it for Monkey. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||01-01-2000||06:24 PM||||To be honest, guys, I wasn't sure how well it would turn out, either.  I think it's a winner.  <P>DXR_DAD--It would be simple to change it to just about anything you want.  You'd just have to send me a good pic of what you wanted.  The only way to change designs once it's on the car would be to change outer (clear) tail light lenses.  It is possible to remove the vinyl, but you would ruin it if you did.  If you had an extra set of lenses, you could have a set for your car shows and another for daily use.<P>I didn't actually remove the grille as it's an integral part of the red insert.  What I did was to buff/grind the black paint off of the insert with a Dremel tool.  I did a quick job and took off some of the plastic, but the next time I do one (on my '85 GT-whenever I get it!), I'll take more time and do it right.  Maybe polish the plastic under where the black paint was so it stays shiny.  I would imagine that it would be just as easy to do on the fastback tail lights, but I don't have a set of those to look at, so I'm not positive.  If anyone has a set of fastback tail lights (complete, but broken is fine) that they want to donate, I'd be happy to make these for those, too.  I'd need the entire assy (one side) including the inner reflector set up and I could send it back once it got done.  If anyone's interested in that email me and we can work something out.  I was wrong about the price, too.  I was envisioning using something else instead of the original red inserts.  I think I could sell these for around $15US (+ shipping).  I don't know what it would cost for a fastback, but I would assume it would be approx the same.  If there is enough interest, I'll see about selling this.  Glad you like it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||dogtired||01-03-2000||03:44 PM||||Those are GREAT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Wasn't it just a couple weeks ago you were asking how to take them apart?<BR>Now how about a rotating message, where we could tell people what we think about them when we pass them???<BR>Great Job!   Animals R US!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||Monkeyman||01-03-2000||08:31 PM||||Actually, dog, there was a LCD bulliten board thing on eBay recently that fit in the back window and displayed whatever message you typed into it.  I bid on it, but was outbidded at the last minute.  The seller gave some examples of what you could put on it like: "For Sale" or "Have a nice day".  I was thinking more on the lines of:  "Where'd you learn to drive, Moron" or "This is NOT an import".<P>Animals in '04!!!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-03-2000||08:39 PM||||"Outbidded" is NOT a word.  I meant to say, "outbid".  Really! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Sorry, but I'm worn out and my feet hurt/smell bad.  I got to go back to work today and I seemed to have forgotten how tough it is to stand on concrete for 9 hours! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Would anyone be interested in buying my "kit"?  It would include the stick on (professional grade) vinyl for both sides.  I can guarantee the price would be $15 (+shipping) for the version shown or for a single "FIERO" across each side.  I assume that anything else (within reason) would be the same, but I would have to double check on that before I made any promises.  I might (?) need a good (clear) image of anything other than text.  It all depends on what the shop has on their computer.  If anyone's interested, please email me.  I'm open to 1 order or 1000!||||reg||11
